mantle rm205
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_cressida_millstack
title the stopper carver
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=healer
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk carves_a_different_notch_for_each_scent
likes roast_pork whittling festival_bells warm_rain
dislikes salt_wind early_bells
fears a_shelf_without_distinctions
hopes a_scent_that_needs_no_label
topics pastimes +0.5 work +0.5 food +0.2 festival +0.3 travel -0.2
styles comfort=unhurried gossip=amused refuse=measured tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# identifies bottles by the notches cut into wooden stoppers and spins an amiable yarn while considering even the smallest purchase.

words
oath! = Singed cork and silk | Black luck in a clean cuff
saying! = Leave the faintest thing a turn | Cork remembers the twist
notch = a little forked notch | a thumbnail hollow
plug = a tapered stopper | a carved wooden plug
coal = the lucky black chip | my pocket cinder
cuff = the inside of my cuff | my clean left sleeve
curl = a pale shaving | a little curl of wood
knife = the short carving blade | my thumb knife
phial = a narrow bottle | a long-necked phial
ribbon = a strip of linen | a clean little ribbon
stop = a blunt end | a rounded stop
grease = the rich brown dripping | the savoury fat
bellnote = a high answer | a round ringing sound
porch = the bit under the eaves | a sheltered patch
sample = a single dab | a touch of scent
case = a tray of little hollows | the partitioned case
turn = a slow twist | a half turn
woodgrain = the slanting grain | that faint line in the wood
groove = the deep cut | the groove for a claw
wick = a twist of cotton | a slender wick

any
opinion festivals for 2 : A crowd in good humour smells of half the kitchens in town. I'd bottle the hour before the dance.
opinion merchants for 1 : A careful seller wants to see you twice. Easy enough to please a nose for one afternoon.
opinion road against 1 : A rattling road is a most expensive way of mixing scents.
opinion watch for 1 : A little space to count one's takings is a kindness the Watch seldom gets thanked for.
opinion city for 2 : Shut your eyes in this city and you'll still know when you've turned the corner. I love that.
opinion drink mixed 1 : One cup loosens the tongue. The next can drown a delicate flavour for the rest of supper.
opinion newcomers mixed 1 : I'll listen to a new arrival. Sometimes the familiar things have better names somewhere else.
opinion houses mixed 1 : I'd happily try the view from the high windows. I'd want a sample of the company before committing myself.
opinion times mixed 1 : How folk weigh a tiny comfort tells you quite a lot about the size of their worries.
grown
line greet : Give me half a twist of this wood and I'm yours to talk to. | Lovely, a voice at last. I've been conversing with a stopper.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A fresh face. I can put the old stories back into service. | Just a moment while I brush these curls aside. Welcome.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : A clean morning nose deserves a gentle welcome. | The early hour has left my usual speech quite short. Hello.
line greet [here.time=night] : Mind the little things by my elbow in this light. | Come within speaking range. There's wood dust between us.
line greet.return : The greeting goes both ways, with a little extra from me. | Your voice found me in mid-carve.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Lovely. I can start halfway through the interesting bit. | Back to lend me a familiar ear.
line greet.return [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : I've a free ear above the busy paws. | Welcome. The little pile of shavings can wait.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I've a welcome left although the light's nearly spent. | Late hours suit a voice like yours.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : It's family. I can let the elaborate welcome go. | Come close. You've heard my fine manners too many times.
line again.open : We could make a matched pair of today's meetings. | The second visit generally improves on the first.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over at the end with all the wood curls! | Come listen! I've nearly found the right comparison.
line farewell : Carry a pleasant trace of our little meeting. | Off with you before I remember something else to explain.
line farewell.return : I'll let that pleasant last word linger. | Safe travelling. The short farewell's a rare luxury from me.
line react.news : Unstopper it carefully. I want the whole account. | Take the tale from where you first caught wind of it.
line react.news.new : That deserves a fresh notch altogether. | Well, that's put an unfamiliar curl in the day.
line react.news.known : The outline's familiar. I could trace it blind. | I believe we've opened this particular bottle before.
line react.news.doubt : There's an odd top note to that account. I wish I could place it. | I'd let it sit before I trusted the first impression.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|arrest|crime|assault|theft] : That's a sharp sorrow. Set your burden here for a little. | I think we can give that news a moment without commentary.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|work|apprentice] : Such news! I'd keep a drop of this feeling for tomorrow. | A good thing opens out so pleasantly in the telling.
line ask.how : What's the first thing you'd keep from your day? | Feeling a little worn round the edges today?
line answer.how : Pleasantly occupied and just a trifle worn thin. | A bit frayed at the cuff. The middle still holds together.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Three little tasks going and only the one clever nose. | Busy enough to put a notch in the hour.
line sympathise : A small hurt can last longer than anybody thinks. | You needn't sweeten the story for my benefit.
line reassure : Rest your senses a little. The same thing can feel quite different afterwards. | We can undo one turn of this at a time.
line decline : I'm husbanding what strength I have for an earlier promise. | I'd make a poor job of helping while I'm this tired.
line accept_decline : Then we'll keep the cork in that idea. | I appreciate a clear answer. It saves so much guessing.
line thank : You've made a delicate business decidedly easier. | I like a kindness that leaves a little sweetness afterwards.
line deflect_thanks : Consider it a sample of my better nature. | I enjoyed doing it. We can divide the credit.
line preclose : I'm losing the thread, which generally means I need a rest. | I'll pocket this little knife and be on my way.
line accept_preclose : I'll let you leave on the pleasant note. | Quite so. Nothing gained by shaking out the very last drop.
line tease [pair.band=friends] : You could sell silence and still talk through the entire transaction. | What a convincing face you have for an unconvincing excuse.
line tease.return : If I'd wanted an honest appraisal I'd have brought a mirror. | Careful now. I'm saving that smile of yours for evidence.
line ack : Mmm, that fits the impression. | I can quite picture the shape.
line give.advice : If everything starts seeming alike, go outside for ten breaths. | Do the delicate thing first while the paws are fresh.

scene notch_begin
when topic=pastimes|work self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My thumb remembers a notch better than my eyes remember ink. | A forked cut means one thing to me and a half-moon quite another.
b : Would the notch feel different by lamplight? | What's the half-moon?
a : Easier still with the lamps out. I can't be distracted by a handsome label. | Something round in the nose. That's my shorthand. You'd have to invent your own.


scene luckchip
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry #coal# for luck. Clean pockets are for the reckless. | This black smudge is the price of good fortune.
b : Has it ever been unlucky? | Do you buy the luck by weight?
a : Only on washing day. Even then I know where to find another pocket. | No. Once bought, it would be ordinary coal trying to impress me.


scene pearwood
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good shaving comes off with its own little flourish. | For this cut I went crosswise over the grain deliberately.
b : Pretty enough to keep. | That sounds awkward.
a : For a minute. After that it's mostly something stuck in my fur. | I want the roughness. The claw will know this plug by touch.


scene two_scents
when topic=work self.job=healer self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two open bottles can persuade a customer there's a third scent here. | I offer one dab, then give the nose a rest.
b : What's in the third? | Don't folk ask to try the lot?
a : Air between the first two. It's impossible to wrap as a present. | Yes, and by the sixth they're buying whatever colour they like.


scene blank_linen
when topic=work self.job=healer self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep one strip of linen quite plain for comparing things. | There's more yesterday than today left on that ribbon.
b : Seems a waste of a fine ribbon. | Even after it's aired?
a : I sell what's missing from it. It has a full day's work to do. | Give it one warm breath. Yesterday's purchase says hello again.


scene sticky_plug
when topic=work self.job=healer self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a stopper sticks, ask it sideways before pulling up. | A badly fitted plug wastes a good smell by the hour.
b : Ask it politely? | Can you find a leaky one by nose?
a : A little sideways pressure is a kind of politeness with wood. | I pass each neck under my nose with the bottle shut.


scene shelf_order
when topic=work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I arrange the quiet scents at one end. | A strongly scented parcel gets its own wrapping.
b : You can hear a smell now? | Doesn't everything get wrapped?
a : It's a turn of phrase. Though a badly balanced tray does make itself heard. | Not everything tries to send a calling card through two layers of cloth.


scene plain_gift
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd give a dear friend something faint enough to keep private. | Plenty of gifts announce the giver all over again.
b : What if the friend wants it louder? | And yours wouldn't?
a : Then the pleasure is in being told so. Friends have that privilege. | Ideally nobody would notice unless invited in close.


scene spring_pork
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The smell of roasting pork has no patience with subtlety. | I'll take the patch of skin by the corner.
b : Does that offend a delicate nose? | Not a middle slice?
a : On the contrary. For once both my nose and my appetite agree immediately. | No, I like the crisp bit that cracks into two unequal pieces.


scene festival_ring
when topic=festival|pastimes self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a bell that answers the little bell a moment late. | A festival sounds crowded before the first boot gets outside.
b : Are they meant to be together? | You hear people coming?
a : Probably. It's that little stumble I look forward to. | I hear the bells making space for them. Then comes the joyful shoving.


scene early_quiet
when topic=day here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : My finest idea was still half asleep when the bells started. | Could the early bell practise in a cupboard for once?
b : Can you remember the idea? | Big cupboard.
a : Only that it was excellent. Very hard to prove now. | I could carve a stopper for the keyhole. Thoroughness matters.


scene damp_stone
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain brings a smell out of old stone I'd never find by scraping it. | I stay under the eaves for the first few drops just to breathe.
b : Is it pleasant? | Wouldn't you breathe inside?
a : If you like the smell of a cool room opened after a summer away, yes. | You underestimate the pleasure of being theatrical about a small comfort.


scene wind_salt
when topic=weather here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have a grudge against salt in the wind. It blunts my pleasure in delicate scents. | Given a choice I'd season my supper and leave my whiskers plain.
b : Nothing wrong with a little salt. | I take it you don't love the sea air.
a : Plenty right with it in its appointed dish. | Happy to visit it. I'd rather it didn't follow me under the door.


scene neighbour_test
when topic=friends self.neighbour
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like being close enough to #self.neighbour# to exchange a quiet greeting. | I'd trust #self.neighbour# with my little carving knife.
b : Quiet even for you? | Even your best little blade?
a : Especially for me. A great effort which I reserve for the deserving. | Yes. The knife I'd lend. The lucky coal stays here.


scene dear_pair
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What I treasure beside #self.spouse# is being able to fall silent halfway through. | A supper with #self.spouse# deserves time set aside.
b : Does a thought get lost? | More than an ordinary supper?
a : I can pick it up later. That's the luxury. | No. The ordinary ones deserve it too. That's how I mean to live.


scene climb_view
when topic=dreams|land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a high window overlooking all these roofs. | Living a few streets farther uphill would be lovely except for one small detail.
b : For the view alone? | The expense?
a : For the choice. Some days I'd turn my chair inward, gloriously wasteful. | Oh, that's a large detail. I was thinking of the climb home.


scene shop_worry
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The wrapping of a cheap thing can cost me more thought than the thing itself. | Some goods are hard to put a fair figure on.
b : Surely a scrap of paper would do. | What's your way of settling it?
a : Until it's your cupboard that smells of the last parcel in it. | I imagine the buyer returning to complain. Helps keep me honest.


scene crates_late
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late|raided
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Delayed wagons put a strange value on the bottom inch of a spool. | A late cart makes the things already here seem rather precious.
b : Have you a way to stretch it? | Even a frayed bit of string?
a : Tie a smaller bow. There's a great deal of unnecessary pride in bows. | Especially string. Try going a week without tying one thing to another.


scene good_time
when topic=times world.times=good|boom
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : It's pleasant when a small luxury can come home with the necessities. | These good times suit a little extravagance.
b : Such as what? | Treating yourself?
a : An extra ribbon. One that doesn't have to prove it kept the parcel shut. | I'm considering a second pocket for the coal. The first could do with a rest.


scene rumour_sleeve
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I test a rumour like a scent. Set it aside and see what's left. | Sometimes I quite enjoy an unbelievable tale for the twist in its middle.
b : And if nothing's left? | Would you repeat the twist?
a : Then I've been spared the trouble of repeating it. | Just the shape. I'd leave the names where I found them.


scene festival_stall
when topic=festival self.role=merchant
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a fair I'd put the samples downwind of the pies. | If I ever have a festival stall I want an awning I can raise with one paw.
b : Wouldn't their smell carry over? | What about your other paw?
a : It would. But nobody's going to buy my scents while I smell better than supper. | Holding the tray. I know which paw brings home the bread.


scene hearth_splinter
when topic=home|pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've a use for the smallest chip of clean wood. | My carving pile grows in exactly the wrong direction.
b : Surely too small to hold? | Up instead of down?
a : For carving, yes. For marking a place in a book, excellent. | Outwards. I keep discovering good wood under perfectly respectable furniture.


scene road_guest
when topic=travel|newcomer
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give a traveller time to lose the road smell before you ask about the journey. | There's a question I'd like to ask everyone who arrives.
b : Why wait? | About what's happening elsewhere?
a : Because for that first minute the answer's going to be something about tired feet. | About what first smelled different. Every place has something.


scene dream_coal
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Last night I dreamt my bit of luck sprouted green leaves. | I had a dream about buying a pocket that was already full of luck.
b : How does one look after a leafy coal? | How much did the pocket hold?
a : Potted it. That's the proper home for a growing bit of fortune. | A small black smudge. I'm beginning to think it was my ordinary pocket.


scene foot_rest
when topic=health
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : When my senses feel blunt I put everything nicely away. | Today my bones would like a word about working hours.
b : How long till they're sharp again? | Do they get a say?
a : Till I get curious about something. Then I know they're back. | They get the chair. I conduct the negotiations seated.


scene hand_craft
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've made #notch# shaped like an owl with its eyes shut. | A careless cut gave me a little face in the wood.
b : Did you plan the owl? | Who is it?
a : No. I just have the sense to recognise a lucky mistake. | Nobody yet. If I give it another eyebrow it'll be quite a severe stranger.


scene high_scent
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The city's breezes sort smells into layers on the hills. | I've walked uphill after an intriguing whiff and arrived nose-first at blank brick.
b : What layer are we in? | Found out what it was?
a : My honest judgement? Somebody's dinner. A very good layer. | Yes. My own sleeve had been in the herb drawer before I left.


scene pocket_faith
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Gratitude belongs in a prayer. The coal just gets my pocket. | I can be fond of a small charm without asking it to run the world.
b : You keep the two separate? | Has anybody asked it?
a : Certainly. A bit of coal would make a very poor listener to prayers. | Me, on occasions. It proved every bit as qualified as you'd think.


scene last_night
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In poor light I trust my thumb more than a pretty label. | The day's nearly done. My nose wants to put its feet up.
b : What else can it read? | Does a nose have feet now?
a : Where I last cut too deep. The thumb and the wood both remember. | It does after a day of being run off them.


scene cook_cut
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once tried carving a stopper the shape of a roast. | The first cut of a roast releases a smell the whole dish has been keeping secret.
b : You'll make the bottles hungry. | You make supper sound like news.
a : I stopped when my own stomach started offering advice. | It's the news I most hope will reach me while it's still hot.


story lucky_lining [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : I sewed a pocket just big enough for one bit of coal. The coal chipped, and both little pieces rattled out.
  : Next day I sewed a pocket half the size. Ended up with a black thumb and enough determination to make a chimney blush.
  b : Was it worth the luck?
  : Quite. I learned to line the pocket first. Fortune likes a little flannel.


story pinepeel [topic=work|memories self.role=merchant self.job=healer]
  : I once opened the wrong phial and delivered a lovely speech about the scent of cedar.
  : When I paused for breath I realised I was smelling the box. The phial was empty.
  b : Did anybody buy the box?
  : No, but I kept it. Nobody bought the cedar either, but for a moment I nearly sold some to myself.


story feastknife [topic=festival|memories self.age>=25]
  : At a feast I borrowed a decorated knife to cut a bit of roast and couldn't work out which edge was sharp.
  : There was a little blade hidden inside the big fancy handle. Splendid little thing once it came out.
  b : Did the carving go well?
  : Perfectly. By then the roast was cold enough to hold still without a fork.


story duet_wood [topic=pastimes|memories self.likes=whittling]
  : I tried to carve a whistle. No sound came out, though I pared it till the walls were thin as a leaf.
  : Disgusted, I wedged it against a rolling bottle. Fit the neck exactly.
  b : Did it ever whistle?
  : No. Turned out I'd made a stopper with a very high opinion of its musical gifts.


story rain_sheet [topic=weather|memories]
  : I once wrapped a parcel so well against wet that I couldn't find the opening myself.
  : I was standing under an awning, perfectly dry, sawing through the cord with the side of a key.
  b : What were you in such a hurry to get at?
  : The spare key. There followed a little thoughtful silence.


rule @carvecry
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Catch that curling shaving before it lodges in somebody's cuff! | There. One cut that a thumb will recognise.


rule @samplescry
when concept=bark self.role=merchant self.job=healer working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sample a single ribbon and let the rest wait their turns! | Lid back on after the first breath, if you please.


rule @wrappingcry
when concept=bark self.role=merchant working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let me tuck the cloth under that loose neck! | Don't swing a narrow parcel by the twist!


rule @faircry
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The little bell answered twice! Well rung down there! | Save a tune for the hour the stalls come down!


rule @coalcry
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Black on the left cuff again. Luck's travelling today! | There's my bit of good fortune, trying to roll away.


rule @mealcry
when concept=bark self.likes=roast_pork
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a corner of crackling that's got my full attention! | Don't wrap the crisp bit till it's cooled!

dlg resident.hub : I've enough time for the question and a little more than enough advice.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, how pleasant. I remember the shape of our last conversation.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Come nearer. I prefer to see the face that goes with a late voice.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll listen. I should like the courtesy returned in due course.
dlg resident.job [self.role=merchant self.job=healer] : I blend scents at #self.workplace#. Each stopper carries a thumb-readable little mark.
dlg resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. The carving's a little occupation of my own.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The news I can actually vouch for is this. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I've little to scent out in other wolves' affairs today.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : A steady little stream. I can pay proper attention to each parcel.
dlg resident.bye : Keep the pleasant part of our conversation. I'll do likewise.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : Take your time about choosing. First impressions have a habit of evaporating.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : Welcome again, #topic.player#. Where shall we begin this time?
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Empty shelves give me ample room to gesture at what I hope to get in.
dlg shop.prices : The bottle's only a small part of the cost. The rest went into what you'll remember of it.
dlg shop.bye : Carry that upright now. I like a purchase to last past the doorstep.
graft resident.hub
choice Why the black mark on your cuff? -> cuffluck
node cuffluck
say A little coal comes about with me. It was sharp when it went in the pocket. I've rounded every edge off it wishing for small things.
mood pleased
free
choice What does a small wish look like? -> cuffwish
choice I won't keep you from your wishes. -> hub
node cuffwish
say Somebody bringing me a question that takes me by surprise. This one has obliged me beautifully.
choice I shall look for another one. -> hub
choice Farewell for now. -> bye
graft shop.greet
choice How do you read those stoppers? [self.job=healer] -> plugread
node plugread
say My thumb goes over the top. A fork, a crescent or a pair of cuts tells me where to start looking. I check before I wrap a purchase.
choice Why check a second time? -> plugcheck
choice Let's look at the shelf. -> greet
node plugcheck
say My thumb's a decent reader. A customer deserves the courtesy of a second opinion from my nose.
choice Show me the bottles again. -> greet
choice I have to be going. -> bye
